data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Need scaffold Vite React project. Can use npm create vite@latest . -- --template react? But directory not empty? Contains .git and DESIGN.md. Need maybe create project manually or use npm init vite and overwrite? Vite create may refuse if files exist. We can use npm create vite@latest hello-app -- --template react, but current dir already repo. Could create in subdir then move files. Simpler: manually create package.json, vite.config.js, index.html, src/main.jsx, src/App.jsx, .gitignore, README.md. Then npm install react react-dom, @codesweep-ai/ui latest, vite @vitejs/plugin-react. Need verify package exports. Need read catalog.json and component d.ts to know AppShell exports Header/Footer, Button, Page, Card props. Let's install first then inspect. Need create .gitignore before commit, and package.json not contain latest word; use npm install @codesweep-ai/ui which writes version range. Need ensure not install optional peer deps. Use --no-optional? npm install doesn't install optional peers automatically unless requested. Need likely npm install @codesweep-ai/ui. It may ask for peer deps? optional peer deps aren't installed. Could use --omit=optional? But that applies to optional dependencies, not peer. Use --legacy-peer-deps maybe. Let's start. Create files. We need know npm/node available. Also need @codesweep-ai/ui from registry maybe internal. Let's check npm info."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1789958937,"id":"chatcmpl-1a84365e03c048509edcc13775ddd0ef","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k2p7-code","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

